Frobenius μ∘δ=id requires BOTH μ (monad) AND δ (comonad).
  monad_cantor  has μ  but no δ  → cannot test
  comonad_goedel has δ  but no μ  → cannot test
  lam() plants both simultaneously → Frobenius holds
  d(monad⊗comonad, λ) = 2.2361   → gap is non-zero
  λ must be planted, not assembled.  (PRIMITIVE_THEOREMS §23/§81)

Non-synthesizability (§23/§81):
  d(monad ⊗ comonad, λ) = 2.2361
  λ cannot be assembled from P and G alone.

